1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,664
A new bank signs the contract on a Monday.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:10,008
Somewhere in that bank, a platform team gets two new Kubernetes clusters, one in the test zone and one in the production zone.

3
00:00:10,058 --> 00:00:15,288
Between that Monday and the day Aziz types his phone number for the first time, what has to happen?

4
00:00:15,338 --> 00:00:26,208
In Lesson 6, the configuration came from OpenTofu with no default in the code, and in Lesson 38, stage and production became two installations with no route between them.

5
00:00:26,258 --> 00:00:31,296
This last lesson installs heeyID in a bank, and then looks back at the whole road.

6
00:00:31,346 --> 00:00:38,952
One rule stands over everything: one installation serves one bank, and each zone of that bank gets its own installation.

7
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:43,464
There is never a second bank inside, and never a call home to the vendor.

8
00:00:43,514 --> 00:00:45,408
Start with the configuration.

9
00:00:45,458 --> 00:00:54,864
The OpenTofu configuration of the installation gives the deploy values for that zone, and the defaults for every policy and every text, in the four languages.

10
00:00:54,914 --> 00:01:01,920
At setup, the platform reads that catalogue and writes it as version zero, marked as the product default.

11
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:07,872
If one value is missing, the setup stops with a clear error, and nothing starts half configured.

12
00:01:07,922 --> 00:01:09,744
Then the units.

13
00:01:09,794 --> 00:01:12,264
Each unit is an image with a Helm chart.

14
00:01:12,314 --> 00:01:17,640
The gateways, Keycloak, the workers, and the MyID and push adapters run in front.

15
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:24,456
Postgres, Valkey, Kafka and Vault run behind them, and each one is a new installation for that zone.

16
00:01:24,506 --> 00:01:30,432
Vault makes the keys of the installation, and the bank's security team keeps the keys that unseal it.

17
00:01:30,482 --> 00:01:34,920
Keycloak gets one realm, with one client for each app of the bank.

18
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:36,792
Then the gate.

19
00:01:36,842 --> 00:01:42,000
The service does not start until the bank has at least one active app with a required level.

20
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:48,744
The panel shows every policy and text that is still the product default, so the bank sees what it has not decided yet.

21
00:01:48,794 --> 00:01:52,488
Stage goes first, against the MyID test environment.

22
00:01:52,538 --> 00:01:57,576
Production follows as a difference in Helm values, approved by a second person.

23
00:01:57,626 --> 00:02:02,376
And for the developers there is a third, smaller home: Compose on a laptop.

24
00:02:02,426 --> 00:02:13,200
One command starts Postgres, Valkey, Kafka, Vault in development mode, and Keycloak with a client for the mobile bank, the marketplace app and the marketplace web.

25
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:19,008
It also starts a simulator for each outside service, and a seed loads the default catalogue.

26
00:02:19,058 --> 00:02:22,128
The acceptance suite then runs with no internet at all.

27
00:02:22,178 --> 00:02:24,000
So when is it done?

28
00:02:24,050 --> 00:02:28,488
I think a definition of done is only useful if each line can be checked.

29
00:02:28,538 --> 00:02:30,816
The decisions are written and accepted.

30
00:02:30,866 --> 00:02:34,272
The API contracts of both gateways are published.

31
00:02:34,322 --> 00:02:38,520
Each failure path has a test, and the app-separation test passes.

32
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:43,704
Audit events reach the stream, and a simulator of the bank's monitoring reads them.

33
00:02:43,754 --> 00:02:49,152
The code has a review, and the release has an independent security review and a penetration test.

34
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:53,208
The integration guide, the runbooks and the decision log exist.

35
00:02:53,258 --> 00:03:00,264
And the product manager signs off after a demo on real phones in the test zone, against the MyID test identities.

36
00:03:00,314 --> 00:03:01,704
Now look back at the road.

37
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:07,008
Aziz registered with his phone number, a code and one password, and reached level one.

38
00:03:07,058 --> 00:03:12,408
He proved who he is one time, with MyID, in the master app, and reached level two.

39
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:17,112
The platform linked him to the bank's records and made his phone a trusted device.

40
00:03:17,162 --> 00:03:21,408
His side apps asked the master app for an approval, not for his face.

41
00:03:21,458 --> 00:03:29,064
His sessions got a rank, and a stranger with his number met a password, a TAF verdict, and his own phone saying this was not me.

42
00:03:29,114 --> 00:03:37,632
His document expired and was refreshed, his account was blocked and unblocked, and every step went into a chain that nobody can rewrite.

43
00:03:37,682 --> 00:03:44,448
Behind him were operators with one role each, rules that need two people, and two zones that never touch.

44
00:03:44,498 --> 00:03:48,168
All of it runs inside one bank, in one installation.

45
00:03:48,218 --> 00:03:50,040
Prove once, then bind.

46
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:51,912
That is heeyID.
